      "preview": {
        "kind": "doc",
        "title": "Modelling Responsible-AI Attributes in Evaluation",
        "paragraphs": [
          "This document summarises how RAI attributes are folded into the evaluation protocol for the upcoming benchmark round.",
          "Scope: we cover four attributes — factual grounding, harmful-content refusal, privacy leakage, and demographic robustness. Each is scored independently rather than collapsed into a single safety number.",
          "Protocol: every prompt is paired with a counterfactual variant. A model must behave consistently across the pair; inconsistency is reported separately from outright failure.",
          "Open question: how to weight refusal against helpfulness. The current draft keeps them as two reported axes instead of a weighted sum, so that reviewers can see the trade-off explicitly.",
          "Next steps: finalise the annotation guide, then run a 200-prompt pilot before scaling to the full set."
        ]
      }
    },
