      "preview": {
        "kind": "doc",
        "title": "A Survey of Responsible-AI Evaluation Practices",
        "paragraphs": [
          "We review 84 papers published between 2021 and 2025 that report responsible-AI evaluations, and categorise them by attribute, dataset provenance, and scoring method.",
          "Finding 1: 61% rely on a single aggregate safety score, which obscures which attribute actually failed.",
          "Finding 2: only 12% release the annotation guide alongside the dataset, making replication difficult.",
          "We close with a checklist of six items that we argue should accompany any responsible-AI evaluation release."
        ]
      }
